Item #:  SCP-5422

Object Class:  Euclid

Special Containment Procedures:  SCP-5422 is currently contained by tracking its movement with the use of Foundation satellites. A method of permanent containment is currently undergoing research.

Description:  SCP-5422 is a UFO of unknown variety or origin. It appears to be a large bubble, measuring roughly 2 meters in length. It is highly mobile, though it never strays from an altitude of approximately 1km/h, though this is not constant and it can gradually alter its speed and direction. SCP-5422 always moves towards the nearest cloud. Darker clouds are always chosen over lighter ones, and as such, it typically is found in rain.

There appears to be a dark object resting inside of SCP-5422. It is hypothesized to be the source of SCP-5422’s locomotion. However, its function and origin are also unknown.

SCP-5422 is believed to have been first spotted as early as 1971. It came to the Foundation’s attention in 2011, after repeated reports of a bubble-like UFO were followed up on. Due to the overwhelming number of false UFO claims from civilians, the use of amnestic treatment for witnesses was not deemed necessary.

