Item #:  SCP-5422

Object Class:  Neutralized

Incident Report:  On October 4th, 2011, an attempt to permanently contain SCP-5422 was made. Foundation operatives pinpointed the location of SCP-5422 and moved in to capture it with the use of aircraft. Shortly after, SCP-5422 ruptured from below and released the previously mentioned dark object from within. Attempts to catch the object were unsuccessful. The subsequent search for the object in the Pacific Ocean was unsuccessful. After releasing its contents, SCP-5422 slowed to a stop and floated in place. It was retrieved for study and is now held in storage.

Description:  SCP-5422 is a deflated uterus of extrasolar origin. Its biological components have been analyzed and traced back to the planet XC-196-H5 in the Andromeda galaxy, which vanished at an indeterminate time between 1957 and 1962. The planet is believed to have entered an unstable orbit, which caused it to exit its solar system. SCP-5422 is believed to have originated from an intelligent organism alive on XC-196-H5 prior to its orbital instability.

In addition to its biological components, SCP-5422 has been augmented with technological components, including a small computer. The computer is programmed to locomote SCP-5422 into specific weather and thermal conditions, presumably to aid the growth of the child.

The precise method by which SCP-5422 became present on Earth is still unknown. However, it is known that the intelligent life on XC-196-H5 possessed more advanced technological capabilities compared to that of an average human, and it is thus hypothesized that SCP-5422 was sent by a form of teleportation.

The ongoing search for the fetus that was once present inside of SCP-5422 remains unsuccessful.




